The last thought that keeps running through your head\:\
Your last encounter with someone you considered your best friend.
You have been coming to him off and on with this non-specific issue you called depression, and he is generous in offering to hear and help each time, but there is only so much he can do for your misguided soul. He is lightyears across from you.
Hidden deep within the protocols of code, the equivalent of coffee stains on programming. You become reluctant once again, you offer to even put it off for tomorrow. This was your biggest mistake. He is  gone now.
Before you know it, you are left in shock for what felt like weeks. There is such a whirlwind of heavy feelings that to this very moment, there is no clear definition for what was right or wrong.
No one dares dream of their greatest colligue in ventures to leave them. It has happened millions of times, to millions more people in the world. It is not special, more forgotten beasts rear their head.
How long has it been since that moment passed? What doors did you open then to allow for solutions to pour through? They are stuck open with draft.
Whar do you define as real?
